WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.000
- [Ted] Kids, I'm gonna tell
you an incredible story.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.720
The story of how I met your mother.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.553
Here I go, or--

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.720
- I'm exhausted, it was
finger painting day at school

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.936
and a five year old boy,
got to second base with me.

00:00:18.936 --> 00:00:20.450
(audience laughing)

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.400
A man with more emotional endurance

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.150
than anyone I know, it was a long,

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:32.985
difficult road, thank
God we finally got here.

00:00:32.985 --> 00:00:34.010
- Here, here.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.490
- [All] Here, here.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.480
- Hey, so you know how I've always

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.787
had a thing for half-Asian girls?

00:00:37.787 --> 00:00:39.880
(audience laughing)

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.987
Well now I've got a new
favorite, Lebanese girls.

00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:43.970
(audience laughing)

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:45.959
Lebanese girls are the new half-Asians.

00:00:45.959 --> 00:00:47.290
(audience laughing)

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.300
- Congrats.
- Right, yeah, thanks.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.570
A kid, I'm tired.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.100
(audience laughing)

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.420
But, she's awesome.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.253
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.433
Daddy's home.

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:02.757
- Wow, you're cooking?

00:01:02.757 --> 00:01:04.187
- Yes I am.

00:01:04.187 --> 00:01:05.020
- Aw.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.360
- Do you have any idea what happened,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.950
right here, in this very bar?

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.333
- No, what happened?

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.990
- Just, all kinds of stuff.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.688
- Are we being punished for something?

00:01:25.688 --> 00:01:26.870
(audience laughing)
- [Ted] No.

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.740
- Yeah, is this gonna take a while?

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:29.573
- Yes.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.970
All right, I'll give her a call.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:33.803
- Do it.

00:01:33.803 --> 00:01:34.636
- I am.

00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:35.555
- Call her.

00:01:35.555 --> 00:01:36.430
(audience laughing)
- I'm calling her.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:37.351
- Great.

00:01:37.351 --> 00:01:40.503
(audience laughing)
- Here I go.

00:01:40.503 --> 00:01:43.670
♪ Which I never knew. ♪

00:01:46.852 --> 00:01:50.102
- Hi, one ticket to Farhampton, please.

00:01:53.635 --> 00:01:57.218
Funny how, sometimes,
you just find things.

00:02:02.958 --> 00:02:03.791
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:11.940
- Hi.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.673
- Let me guess, Ted.

00:02:14.673 --> 00:02:15.508
(audience laughing)

00:02:15.508 --> 00:02:17.495
(casual music)

00:02:17.495 --> 00:02:19.855
All right, home sweet home.

00:02:19.855 --> 00:02:21.188
Wait one second.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:25.580
Okay, stay, we'll work on that.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.910
(buzzer buzzing)

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:32.483
Television, display front door security.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:34.670
Television display--

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:35.965
Oh, for Pete sakes.

00:02:35.965 --> 00:02:39.320
♪ May come and go ♪

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:44.320
♪ Crooked dreams, they always glow ♪

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:50.040
♪ Remember, remember ♪

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:55.700
♪ All we fight for ♪

00:02:56.784 --> 00:02:59.867
♪ Remember, remember ♪

